diff --git a/svc/docs/API.md b/svc/docs/API.md
index d96c758..0f37806 100644
--- a/svc/docs/API.md
+++ b/svc/docs/API.md
@@ -6,5 +6,19 @@
 | GET | /users | All users, by id. |
 | GET | /users/<id> | One user, or 404. |
 | POST | /users | Create a user from `{name, email}`. 201, 400 on invalid input, 409 if the email is taken. |
+| POST | /users/import | Create many users, all or nothing. See below. |
+
+### POST /users/import
+
+Body: `{"users": [{"name": ..., "email": ...}, ...]}`, at most 100 entries. Each entry is validated like `POST /users`. If any entry fails, no user is created.
+
+| Status | Body | When |
+|---|---|---|
+| 201 | `{"users": [...]}` in input order | All entries created. |
+| 400 | `{"errors": [{"index": i, "errors": [...]}]}` | An entry is invalid or not an object. A missing, empty or non-list `users` gives `{"errors": [{"error": "users must be a non-empty list"}]}`. |
+| 409 | `{"errors": [{"index": i, "error": "email already registered"}]}` | An email already exists in the service, or repeats an earlier entry in the batch (`index` is the later entry). Emails are compared ignoring capitalisation. |
+| 413 | `{"error": "at most 100 users per request"}` | More than 100 entries. |
+
+Validation (400) is checked before duplicates (409).
 
 A user is `{id, name, email}`.
